.TH SNAKE 1 "October 2026" "snake 1.0.9" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
snake \- professional terminal snake game for developers
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B snake
[\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.br
.B snake play
[\fB\-m\fR, \fB\-\-mode\fR \fImode\fR]
[\fB\-d\fR, \fB\-\-difficulty\fR \fIlevel\fR]
[\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-size\fR \fIpreset|WxH\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-theme\fR \fIname\fR]
[\fB\-\-direct\fR]
[\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-obstacles\fR]
[\fB\-\-resume\fR]
[\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIms\fR]
[\fB\-\-screen\-reader\fR]
[\fB\-\-hardware\-udp\fR \fIaddr\fR]
.br
.B snake daily
[\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-theme\fR \fIname\fR]
.br
.B snake stats
[\fB\-\-json\fR | \fB\-\-csv\fR]
.br
.B snake replay
[\fIfile\fR]
[\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIms\fR]
[\fB\-\-verify\fR]
.br
.B snake bot
[\fB\-\-headless\fR]
[\fB\-\-ticks\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-\-speed\fR \fIms\fR]
[\fB\-\-seed\fR \fIN\fR]
[\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-theme\fR \fIname\fR]
.br
.B snake config
[\fB\-\-edit\fR | \fB\-\-reset\fR]
.br
.B snake \-\-version
.br
.B snake \-\-help

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B snake
is a professional, developer-grade terminal Snake game engineered for coffee breaks.
It installs in one command, launches in under 5 milliseconds, uses double-buffered
flicker-free rendering with alternate-screen isolation, and restores the terminal state cleanly
under all exit conditions.

The underlying simulation engine is 100% deterministic, enabling shareable level seeds,
recorded input playback, autonomous AI testing, and headless verification.

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B play
Start an interactive game of Snake. If no command is provided, \fBplay\fR is executed by default.
.TP
.B daily
Play today's global Daily Challenge. The seed is deterministically generated from the current UTC date
so that every player around the world encounters the exact same food spawns and procedural obstacles.
.TP
.B stats
Display local lifetime metrics, high scores per mode, top 50 leaderboard entries, and unlocked achievements.
Outputs can be formatted as JSON (\fB\-\-json\fR) or CSV (\fB\-\-csv\fR).
.TP
.B replay \fR[\fIfile\fR]
Play back a recorded game file (.snk). If no file is specified, the latest recorded game
at \fI~/.config/snake/replays/latest.snk\fR is loaded. Pass \fB\-\-verify\fR to run a headless determinism
check that asserts the exact final score, length, and tick count match the recording.
.TP
.B bot
Launch the autonomous AI autopilot using BFS pathfinding and tail-escape heuristics.
In default visual mode, the AI plays itself on screen. In \fB\-\-headless\fR mode, the bot simulates
up to 1,500 ticks at over 7,500 ticks per second for automated benchmarking and CI regression testing.
.TP
.B config
Display the active configuration and key bindings. Use \fB\-\-edit\fR to open \fI~/.config/snake/config.toml\fR
in your \fB$EDITOR\fR, or \fB\-\-reset\fR to revert to default settings.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-m ", " \-\-mode " \fImode\fR"
Select game mode: \fBclassic\fR (default), \fBtime\-attack\fR, \fBsurvival\fR, or \fBzen\fR.
.TP
.BR \-s ", " \-\-size " \fIpreset|WxH\fR"
Select board dimensions preset: \fBsmall\fR (20×12), \fBmedium\fR (28×16), \fBclassic\fR (24×20, default), or \fBlarge\fR (36×20). Custom dimensions may also be passed as \fIWIDTHxHEIGHT\fR (e.g. \fI30x15\fR).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-difficulty " \fIlevel\fR"
Select difficulty preset: \fBeasy\fR (160ms/tick), \fBnormal\fR (110ms/tick), \fBhard\fR (75ms/tick), or \fBinsane\fR (45ms/tick with procedural obstacles).
.TP
.B \-\-direct
Bypass the interactive main menu and launch gameplay immediately.
.TP
.B \-\-seed " \fIN\fR"
Initialize the pseudo-random number generator with a deterministic 64-bit integer seed.
.TP
.BR \-t ", " \-\-theme " \fIname\fR"
Visual theme: \fBdark\fR (default neon), \fBlight\fR, \fBhigh\-contrast\fR, \fBcolorblind\fR, or \fBcorporate\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-obstacles
Generate symmetrical or scattered procedural obstacles based on the seed.
.TP
.B \-\-resume
Automatically restore an unfinished game from \fI~/.config/snake/save.json\fR (default true).
.TP
.B \-\-speed " \fIms\fR"
Override the tick interval in milliseconds (e.g. 150 for relaxed pace, 60 for fast-paced).
.TP
.B \-\-screen\-reader
Enable accessible plain text stream mode for screen readers.
.TP
.B \-\-hardware\-udp " \fIaddr\fR"
Listen on a UDP address (e.g. \fI:4242\fR) for directional packets sent by an external ESP8266 or ESP32 joystick.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Export statistics and leaderboard as formatted JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-csv
Export leaderboard records as comma-separated values.
.TP
.B \-\-verify
Run headless determinism verification during replay playback.
.TP
.B \-\-headless
Run the AI bot in headless non-interactive mode at maximum CPU speed.
.TP
.B \-\-ticks " \fIN\fR"
Maximum number of ticks to simulate in headless bot mode (default 1500).

.SH BOARD SIZES
Snake CLI provides four curated board size presets tailored for different terminal pane configurations:
.TP
.B small (20×12 cells, 40×12 terminal chars)
Compact layout designed for split panes, status bars, and small laptop windows.
.TP
.B medium (28×16 cells, 56×16 terminal chars)
Balanced playground offering quick turnaround and brisk reflex dynamics.
.TP
.B classic (24×20 cells, 48×20 terminal chars)
Authentic retro arcade aspect ratio. Default setting.
.TP
.B large (36×20 cells, 72×20 terminal chars)
Expansive widescreen arena for extended runs, high scores, and massive snake lengths.

.SH GAME MODES
.TP
.B classic
Authentic Snake rules. Collisions with walls or the snake's own body result in Game Over.
.TP
.B time\-attack
Begins with a 60-second countdown timer. Each food item consumed adds +3 seconds of bonus time and higher score points.
The game ends when the timer reaches zero or a fatal collision occurs.
.TP
.B survival
Dynamic shrinking arena. Every 50 ticks, the perimeter walls contract inward by 1 unit on each side.
.TP
.B zen
Stress-free, meditative mode. Border collisions wrap around to the opposite side of the grid,
and the snake passes harmlessly through its own body. No Game Over state is possible.

.SH POWER-UPS & SPECIAL ITEMS
One permanent food apple exists on the grid and respawns immediately when eaten ("one after another"). Concurrently alongside food, 2\(en3 special items appear on the grid (1 guaranteed poison hazard + 1\(en2 power-ups; active effects and board lifespans last 5.0 seconds):
.TP
.B Permanent Food (Single)
Standard food apple that awards points and grows snake length. Exactly one apple exists at a time and respawns immediately upon being eaten ("one after another").
.TP
.B Slow-Mo (⏱)
Halves snake movement speed for 5.0 seconds.
.TP
.B Ghost (👻)
Enters Zen Mode for 10.0 seconds: walls do not stop the game (wrap-around), obstacles are phased through, and full body overlap is allowed.
.TP
.B 3x Multiplier (⚡)
Triples all points awarded for 5.0 seconds.
.TP
.B Shrink (✂)
Immediately cuts the snake's length in half upon consumption.
.TP
.B Poison (☠) [Hazard - Avoid!]
Deducts -30 points, adds +1 unrewarded length, and triggers an uncontrollable 5.0-second Toxic Speed Surge (2x speed)!

.SH THE BOSS KEY
Pressing \fBb\fR or \fBEsc\fR instantly conceals the game and displays a convincing fake terminal screen:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBhtop\fR: Animated multi-core CPU meters, memory gauges, load averages, and realistic system process table.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBbuild\fR: Compiling target log stream and passing unit test runners.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBgit\fR: Decorated git commit graph and log history.
.PP
The game automatically pauses and preserves its exact state. Pressing \fBb\fR again immediately returns to the game.
The default boss screen can be configured via \fIdefault_boss_screen\fR in \fIconfig.toml\fR.

.SH KEYBINDINGS
Default controls (customizable in \fI~/.config/snake/config.toml\fR):
.TP
.B Move Up
Up Arrow, W, K
.TP
.B Move Down
Down Arrow, S, J
.TP
.B Move Left
Left Arrow, A, H
.TP
.B Move Right
Right Arrow, D, L
.TP
.B Pause / Resume
P, Space
.TP
.B Boss Key
B, Esc
.TP
.B Restart
R (when Game Over)
.TP
.B Quit
Q, Ctrl+C

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/snake/config.toml
User preferences, default theme, grid dimensions, and custom key bindings.
.TP
.I ~/.config/snake/stats.json
Persistent player metrics, mode high scores, top 50 leaderboard, and unlocked achievements.
.TP
.I ~/.config/snake/save.json
Auto-saved state of any in-progress game. Removed automatically upon game completion.
.TP
.I ~/.config/snake/replays/latest.snk
Gzip-compressed recording of the most recently played game.

.SH IOT HARDWARE CONTROLLER
Snake supports external input via an ESP8266 or ESP32 microcontroller with an analog joystick.
The controller transmits UDP datagrams to the host machine:
.PP
.nf
.RS
snake play --hardware-udp :4242
.RE
.fi
.PP
The protocol accepts 1-byte binary packets (0x01=UP, 0x02=DOWN, 0x03=LEFT, 0x04=RIGHT, 0x05=PAUSE, 0x06=BOSS)
or newline-delimited ASCII strings ("UP\\n", "DOWN\\n", etc.).
See \fIhardware/PROTOCOL.md\fR and \fIhardware/esp8266_snake.ino\fR for firmware and pinout instructions.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Play standard classic mode:
.B snake play
.TP
Play survival mode with the colorblind-safe theme:
.B snake play \-\-mode survival \-\-theme colorblind
.TP
Participate in today's daily challenge:
.B snake daily
.TP
View local leaderboard and unlocked achievements:
.B snake stats
.TP
Verify determinism of a recorded game replay:
.B snake replay \-\-verify
.TP
Run headless AI benchmark for 1000 ticks:
.B snake bot \-\-headless \-\-ticks 1000

